                        <locus target="#9r">-9r</locus>اِنَّ اللهَ كَانَ غَفُوْراً رَّحِيْماً<note>The folio is loose and placed, front to back, between folios 8 and 10.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>3:92-4:23. The final folio is loose, numbered 9. Red dots or commas as verse markers. First line of the ǧuz', as well as some other words and sentences are written in large hand and enhanced in red. Fol. 12 is from another hand, using ihmāl marks (rā') and black triple dots as verse markers. Extensions of letters into the margin; several words left uncompleted at the end of a line, completed or written in full on the following line. Deletions. Catchwords from another hand, more recent than the matn, and casual.</note>
                     <note/>
